under sleep deprivation for placebo and creatine groups over time." class="r-1ofykva" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="f698d718-52f9-4253-8731-9276bdf117f5" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-nf0n6c"><div data-rid="8bf679ad-fe8b-4d66-bb43-13832165909b" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-a4i6l1 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>2. Chris loves creatine's brain benefits</p></span></div><div data-rid="dd6e6549-3333-4c47-8612-06b17c1a6a8a" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-43ouwb alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>One of the main reasons Chris takes creatine gummies is to improve brain health - he specifically called it out on his podcast in a recent episode! As he pointed out, most people associate creatine with physiological benefits, but in reality the supplement is also very beneficial for your brain.</p><br><p>Research indicates that creatine's <strong>positive impact on cognitive function is even more pronounced during sleep deprivation</strong> (see chart.) When you're as busy as Chris-- podcasts, TV appearances, and philanthropic efforts -- you're likely running low on sleep. That's where creatine can really help.</p></span></div></div></div><div data-rid="b8cd001b-866b-49a2-8db3-dc76b7ee3276" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="creapure" tabindex="-1" id="creapure" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-mdohop"><div data-rid="59eed3b9-b495-47b9-bfe2-6782dfc0a47f" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-q82ubg"><div data-rid="0125abd8-e55b-474b-9683-7069e35ac130" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1lv8kjh alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>3. Creatine is proven to increase strength</p></span></div><div data-rid="54bef34c-ad87-497d-b39a-0b8e01d6bbc0" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1rvfd99 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Chris Long had incredible longevity as an NFL player - <strong>after being picked #2 overall in